## 1. Option Bag Junk Drawer — `describeCheckout` (L10–19)

**Evidence:** *"parameter: options"*, *"6 distinct property reads: currency, plan, region, retry, role, status"*

**What an agent gets wrong today.** The bag is typed, so this isn't a `any` problem — it's a *cohesion* problem. `CheckoutOptions` fuses three unrelated concerns: identity (`plan`, `role`), locale (`region`, `currency`), and attempt state (`status`, `retry`). The function reads all six and joins them positionally into a colon-delimited string. Nothing in the type system says that string is a **format** — but it is: `"pro:owner:us:USD:paid:false"` is a key that things downstream will compare, cache on, or log.

An agent told "add tax region to the checkout description" does the obvious thing: append `taxRegion: string` to the interface and `options.taxRegion` to the array. TypeScript makes every construction site fail, so the agent softens it to `taxRegion?: string` — and now the join silently emits `"pro:owner:us:USD:paid:false:undefined"` for existing callers. The output format changed and nothing failed.

**Refactor.** Two moves. First, destructure at the signature so the six owned fields are visible in the API, not buried in the body (this is the detector's own `name_option_shape` action). Second, separate the *inputs* from the *format*:

```ts
interface CheckoutIdentity { plan: string; role: string }
interface CheckoutLocale   { region: string; currency: string }
interface CheckoutAttempt  { status: string; isRetry: boolean }

export interface CheckoutContext {
  identity: CheckoutIdentity;
  locale: CheckoutLocale;
  attempt: CheckoutAttempt;
}

/** Stable colon-delimited checkout key. Field order and count are part of the contract. */
export function describeCheckout({ identity, locale, attempt }: CheckoutContext): string {
  return [
    identity.plan, identity.role,
    locale.region, locale.currency,
    attempt.status, String(attempt.isRetry),
  ].join(":");
}
```

The grouping is what does the work: an agent adding a tax field now has to pick a group, and the doc comment tells it that widening the array is a contract change. If you want the minimal version instead, just destructuring in the signature plus the `: string` return annotation clears the finding — the grouping is the part that survives the next three edits.

